atory symptoms are consistent with PCD, though absence of situs inversus reduces specificity."]}, "B1.1": {"id": "B1.1", "label": "Cystic Fibrosis", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.109, "danger": 0.6, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Stable growth moderately argues against CF and supports PCD as the underlying diagnosis."]}, "B1.2": {"id": "B1.2", "label": "Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia", "parent": "B1", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.2173312770496272, "posterior": 0.23546239556067242, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Stable growth moderately argues against CF and supports PCD as the underlying diagnosis."], "evidence_against": ["Lack of situs inversus weakens PCD but does not exclude it due to variable ciliary abnormalities."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.8, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.35, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology", "representative_diseases": []}, "B1.3": {"id": "B1.3", "label": "Other Rare Mucociliary Disorders", "level": 2, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.085, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "B1", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}}, "frontier": ["B1.2", "B1.2"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Are the chronic respiratory symptoms and airway dilation on MRI sufficiently non-specific to maintain 'Other Rare Mucociliary Disorders' (B1.3) as a plausible diagnosis?", "summary": "Non-specific findings maintain plausibility for rare mucociliary disorders, but structural abnormalities remain a stronger explanation."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the diastolic murmur best heard at right lower sternal border (option A) provide strong evidence for congenital cardiopulmonary syndromes (B2)?", "summary": "The murmu