intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "confirm"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "refute"}, {"t": 4, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B1.1", "B1.3", "B3"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=40%, source=primekg]\n\nCystic Fibrosis vs Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia:\n  Favours first:  biliary cirrhosis, childhood onset, cirrhosis, clubbing of fingers, cor pulmonale\n  Favours second: abdominal situs inversus, abnormal atrial arrangement, abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal central microtubular pair morphology of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal ciliary motility\n\nNOT typically seen in Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia: abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal sweat electrolytes, decreased fertility, heterotaxy\n\nRelated to Cystic Fibrosis: autosomal recessive disease, respiratory system disease\n\nRelated to Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia: ciliary discoordination due to random ciliary orientation, ciliary dyskinesia with defective radial spokes, ciliary dyskinesia with excessively long cilia\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent bronchopulmonary infections → Cystic Fibrosis\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent respiratory infections → Cystic Fibrosis\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent sinopulmonary infections → Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia"}
